Use case: illustration-story. Asset: a production PIXEL ART game sprite animation atlas, transparent RGBA, 2048x2048 pixels, EXACTLY 16 equal columns by 16 equal rows, 256 frames total. Each cell 128x128. No visible grid, lettering, numbers, backgrounds, floors, props, shadows or particles. Every character entirely inside its cell with ample transparent padding, consistent center x64 and foot baseline y112. One tiny Victamin per cell, including hiding poses. Crisp deliberate pixel clusters and limited cream/ivory/yellow/orange/brown palette, no antialias blur or photographic texture. References1 and2 are ORIGINAL character design authority, not the pixel style. Same recognizable limbless layered paper-square pompom creature, exactly TWO long upright bunny ears with white outer ear, screen-left inner ear ORANGE and screen-right inner ear YELLOW in front-facing views. Orange square cheeks, small dark eyes with white highlights, tiny U mouth. NO arms, hands, legs, feet, claws, tail, hat or human body. Preserve layered flat rectangular cream tiles with scattered yellow tiles, not shaggy fur. Movement is squash/stretch, body hops and ear inertia. All frames stay centered; motion through space is handled by code.
Rows top-to-bottom, each16 columns is one continuous temporal sequence with distinct small incremental drawings:
1 breathing idle, occasional blink, curious ear twitch;
2 looking left then right and alert ears;
3 bouncy travelling cycle facing right three-quarter, paper layers ruffle;
4 low crouch and spring anticipation;
5 jump ascending and apex, ears trail;
6 falling with startled face and raised ears;
7 soft landing squash then recover;
8 being gently held in midair, surprise then calm;
9 suspended wriggling struggle, ears wiggle, NO added limbs;
10 happy head-petting, closed smiling eyes, leaning into touch;
11 sleepy yawning and curling into compact nest shape;
12 sleeping breathing, relaxed ears, no text;
13 wake stretch, yawn then alert, no limbs;
14 proud little heart-bonk bounce and delighted reaction, no hearts drawn;
15 turn away and squeeze down to peek from behind scenery, rear has NO eyes;
16 peek then re-emerge and shake paper layers into place.
Frames1-16 across each row form smooth readable loops or one-shot motion as specified. Maintain character scale, ear color identity and baseline throughout. This is one dense game atlas, not a collage of separate illustrations. No scene or text.
